{
 "manufacturer": "Daikin Applied",
 "manufacturer_slug": "daikin-applied",
 "model": "EWWD-DZ / EWWH-DZ water-cooled chiller, VORTEX software (Daikin Applied Europe)",
 "model_slug": "ewwd-ewwh-dz-bacnet",
 "aliases": [
  "EWWD-DZ",
  "EWWH-DZ",
  "VORTEX",
  "D-EIGOC00103-21EN-DZ"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Water-cooled chiller controller",
 "applies_to": "Daikin Applied Europe EWWD-DZ and EWWH-DZ water-cooled chillers running the VORTEX software (up to three compressors).",
 "summary": "The EWWD-DZ and EWWH-DZ chillers run Daikin's VORTEX software. BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP comes from a POL908/POL904 module. The list covers chiller enable, local/remote, mode, network cool/heat setpoints and capacity and current limits, water temperatures, per-compressor capacity, speed, IGV position, current, power and temperatures for up to three compressors, pump status, and individual alarm objects plus alarm index/code AVs.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP",
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": 1,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "AV 992 is printed for both ChillerVoltage and Comp2AlarmActive; MV 1 is printed for both UnitStatus and CondFlowSwStatus; the object without a confirmed instance is listed without one.",
  "Four rows print an invalid object type and are left out: Comp1OffCmpFault (type \"CS\", instance 322), UnitOFFEvapWaterFlow (701), UnitOFFPhaseVoltage (820) and UnitPwrRestore (515), which print type \"0\".",
  "Several compressor 2 and 3 alarm objects are printed as BI where the matching compressor 1 object is a BV; types are kept as printed.",
  "Binary alarm objects list a third state \"2 = NULL\" in the guide.",
  "Daikin France (Easyspec) publishes this guide as a PDF inside a zip together with the Modbus guide."
 ],
